<p>August 27, 2024:  <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408100.pdf">Third Emergency Proclamation</a> supplements the Governor&#8217;s <a href="https://spo.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/2406149-Telecommunications-on-HHL.pdf">Second Proclamation</a> to address the danger and threat of an emergency related to the loss of phone and internet services to businesses, schools, and other institutions located on Hawaiian Home Lands statewide.  This proclamation suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations. The proclamation will continue through October 26, 2024, unless terminated or suspended by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 26, 2024:  <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408096.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="2">Second emergency proclamation</a> relating to Tropical Storm Hone, to allow continued government response to the impacts of Tropical Storm and Hurricane Hone.  This proclamation covers the County of Hawai&#8217;i.  This disaster emergency relief period shall continue through September 2, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 24, 2024:  <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408076_Fifth-Proclamation-Relating-to-Heavy-Rains-and-Flooding-part-2-signed.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="2">Emergency proclamation</a> relating to Tropical Storm Hone suspends Chapters 103D to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This disaster emergency relief period shall continue through August 26, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 20, 2024:  <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408076_Fifth-Proclamation-Relating-to-Heavy-Rains-and-Flooding-part-2-signed.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="2">Fifth emergency proclamation</a> relating to heavy rains and flooding as a result of emergency conditions created by heavy rains and flooding on Kauai suspends Chapters 103D and 103F, HRS, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This proclamation supersedes all prior proclamations relating to heavy rains and flooding, and that the disaster emergency relief period shall continue through October 19, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 15, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408068_Eighth-Proclamation-Relating-to-Affordable-Housing.pdf">Eighth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to affordable housing suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, to the extent that the department or agency has determined that it is not practicable or advantageous to procure the services required via traditional procurement methods and the procurement promotes the construction, development, redevelopment, repair, renovation, and occupancy of housing.  The disaster emergency relief period shall continue through October 14, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 7, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408029.pdf">Emergency Proclamation</a>, relating to condominium insurance stabilization, suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code, the disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through October 6, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by a separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>August 2, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2408014_Proclamation-Relating-to-School-Bus-Services.pdf">Emergency Proclamation</a>, relating to School Bus Services, suspends Chapter 103D HRS, Hawaii public procurement code, to provide relief for the Department of Education (DOE) school bus service shortage, shall commence immediately and continue through October 1, 2024.</p>
<p>July 19, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Sixteenth-Proclamation-Relating-to-Wildfires.pdf">Sixteenth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to wildfires suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code and Chapter 103F, HRS, purchases of health and human services, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This proclamation supersedes all earlier proclamations relating to wildfires. The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through September 17, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 15, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/2407050_Fifteenth-Proclamation-Relating-to-Wildfires.pdf">Fifteenth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to wildfires suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code and Chapter 103F, HRS, purchases of health and human services, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This proclamation supersedes all earlier proclamations relating to wildfires. The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through September 13, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 12, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/JUL-11-2024-Thirteenth-EP-Relating-to-Wildfires.pdf">Fourteenth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to wildfires suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code and Chapter 103F, HRS, purchases of health and human services, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This proclamation supersedes all earlier proclamations relating to wildfires. The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through September 10, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 12, 2024:  <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Proclamation-Relating-to-Kauai-Helicopter-Crash.pdf">Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to Kaua&#8217;i Helicopter Crash suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through July 31, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 11, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/JUL-11-2024-Thirteenth-EP-Relating-to-Wildfires.pdf">Thirteenth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to wildfires suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code and Chapter 103F, HRS, purchases of health and human services, to the extent that compliance results in any additional delays involved in meeting procurement requirements for selecting contractors in a timely manner to respond to emergency situations.  This proclamation supersedes all earlier proclamations relating to wildfires. The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through September 9, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 2, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/2407006.pdf">Fifteenth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to Axis Deer crisis in Maui County, suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code, through August 30, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
<p>July 2, 2024: <a href="https://governor.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/2407005.pdf">Twelfth Emergency Proclamation</a> relating to wildfires in the counties of Honolulu, Hawaii, and Maui, suspends Chapter 103D, HRS, Hawaii public procurement code and Chapter 103F, HRS, purchases of health and human services.  This proclamation supersedes all earlier proclamations relating to wildfires. The disaster emergency relief period shall commence immediately and continue through August 31, 2024, unless terminated or superseded by separate proclamation, whichever shall occur first.</p>
